osing money.", "Its founders got a meeting with Blockbuster's CEO. Their offer: sell Netflix for fifty million dollars.", "He listened. At first, he laughed, and then he followed with a flat no.", "Now the detail almost nobody knows.", "Netflix's founders got the invitation less than twelve hours before the meeting. With the clock against them and almost broke, they spent money they didn't have on a jet, just to hear that no.", "They walked in wearing shorts, flip-flops and a Hawaiian shirt.", "Ten years later, Blockbuster filed for bankruptcy. Netflix became worth billions.", "Today, only one Blockbuster is still alive, in Oregon.", "Lesson: when a small player changes how people buy, take the meeting seriously.", "Tell me if you would have bought it.", "Follow for the next million dollar mistake."], "fuentes": ["https://fortune.com/2023/04/14/netflix-cofounder-marc-randolph-recalls-blockbuster-rejecting-chance-to-buy-it/", "https://ia.acs.org.au/article/2016/netflix-pitched-itself-to-blockbuster-for--50m.html", "https://marketplace.org/2020/09/08/ceo-reed-hastings-on-how-netflix-beat-blockbuster"], "escena": {"momentos": [["s_1", 1, null], ["s_2", 2, null], ["s_3", 3, null], ["s_4", 4, null], ["s_5", 5, null], ["s_6", 6, null], ["s_7", 7, null], ["s_8", 8, null], ["s_9", 9, null], ["s_10", 10, null], ["s_fin", 11, null], ["s_cta", 12, null], ["lost0", 0, "^lost"], ["decision", 0, "^decision"], ["king", 1, "^king"], ["m9000", 1, "^9"], ["dvds", 2, "^dvds"], ["losing", 2, "^losing"], ["m50", 3, "^50"], ["laughed", 4, "^laughed"], ["flat", 4, "^flat"], ["detail", 5, "^detail"], ["hours", 6, "^hours"], ["jet", 6, "^jet"], ["shorts", 7, "^shorts"], ["bankruptcy", 8, "^bankruptcy"], ["billions", 8, "^billions"], ["one", 9, "^one"], ["lesson", 10, "^lesson"]], "escenas": [{"tipo": "pelicula", "desde": "0", "escala": 1.24, "zonas": [{"x0": -300, "x1": 1300, "set": "nocheV", "o": {"ciudad": true, "sem": 51}, "cam": 0}, {"x0": 1300, "x1": 2600, "set": "corporativoV", "o": {